          "heading": "why_in_hospital",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.0",
            "sections.1"
          ],
          "text": "Your child came in at 6 hours old with:\n- fast breathing\n- a high temperature\n- grunting\n\nThe team found that your child had neonatal sepsis (a blood infection in a newborn). This was linked to a positive GBS (Group B Streptococcus) result in this pregnancy and antibiotics given less than 4 hours before delivery."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "The team did a sepsis screen. This included blood tests and a blood culture (a test to look for infection in the blood).\n\nThe blood culture showed no growth at 36 hours and was confirmed negative at 48 hours.\n\nYour child was given two antibiotics through a drip:\n- benzylpenicillin\n- gentamicin\n\nBased on the clinical picture and the blood test results, the team decided to complete a full 5-day course of antibiotics through the drip. The course was completed on day 5.\n\nRoutine newborn checks were done. Your child passed the newborn hearing screen."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.2",
          "heading": "medicines",
